commit (mission branch)

feat(mission): warn at session start when the installed plugin is outdated (#33)

Closes #32

## What

A `SessionStart` hook (matcher `startup`) in the `mission` plugin
compares the installed version with the published one and, when they
differ, shows both SHAs and the update command to the user. Auto-update
stays off; this makes the drift visible.

- `plugins/mission/scripts/check-plugin-version.sh`: installed version =
name of `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` (the cache directory); published version
= `HEAD` of the manifest's `repository`, read with `git ls-remote`;
output as `{"systemMessage": ...}`; fails open with the reason on
stderr.
- `plugins/mission/hooks/hooks.json`: the `SessionStart` entry,
`timeout` 10 s.
- `tests/test_check_plugin_version.py`: runs the declared command
against a synthetic cache entry whose manifest points at a local git
repository, so no network is needed.
- Plugin README (component table and "Warning when the plugin is
outdated"), `docs/INVENTORY.md` (evidence), session summary.

## Decisions

- **Installed version is the marketplace `HEAD` SHA, not the last commit
under `plugins/mission/`.** Verified locally: the cache holds
`mission/f845d1b4e969`, and `f845d1b` (#29) does not touch
`plugins/mission/`. Matches the docs: for a relative path in a
Git-hosted marketplace, the version is "the commit SHA of the installed
directory", 12 characters ([How Claude Code computes the
version](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/loading.md#how-claude-code-computes-the-version)).
- **Compare with `HEAD`, accept docs-only merges.** After a docs-only
merge, `claude plugin update` really does install a new version, so the
warning is accurate. Comparing with the last commit under
`plugins/mission/` would need the GitHub API (rate limits, more moving
parts) for no real gain (KISS).
- **Repository from the manifest's `repository`.** Not hard-coded (would
duplicate the manifest, DRY) and not from `known_marketplaces.json`
(internal file, no documented contract). Assumes the plugin lives in the
marketplace repository it names, as this one does; documented.
- **`systemMessage`, not stdout or `additionalContext`.**
`systemMessage` is the "warning message shown to the user"; on
`SessionStart`, plain stdout and `additionalContext` enter Claude's
context ([Hooks
reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md#sessionstart)) and
would cost tokens every session.
- **Matcher `startup` only.** The loaded version only changes when
Claude Code launches.
- **Timeout 10 s.** Claude's first response waits for `SessionStart`
hooks (same section). Measured on Windows: `git ls-remote` to GitHub
0.5–0.75 s; unresolvable host fails in ~5 s.

## How RED was seen

- `python -m unittest tests.test_check_plugin_version` before the hook:
6 of 6 errored with `KeyError: 'SessionStart'`.
- Mutations seen failing, then undone: always warning → the up-to-date
test failed; `additionalContext` instead of `systemMessage` → the
warning test failed; renaming the manifest key the script reads → the
unreachable-repository test failed.
- Gates: `validate_plugins.py` OK (no warning beyond the omitted
version); `python -m unittest discover -s tests` 15 tests OK (1
pre-existing POSIX-only skip).

## End-to-end check

Real headless session (`claude -p`, CLI 2.1.326, `--plugin-dir` on a
copy of the plugin in a directory named `84b2bf30f3ee`,
`--include-hook-events`): the hook ran as `SessionStart:startup` and
emitted the `systemMessage`; asked whether its context mentions
"desatualizado" or the SHA, the model answered **NO**.

Also ran against the real cache of this repository: `instalado
84b2bf30f3ee, publicado e316a24e9826`.

Both remaining acceptance criteria were then seen:

- [x] **Positive control:** the same probe, with the copy of the script
emitting `additionalContext` instead, answered **YES**; rerun right
after with the real script, **NO**. The probe can detect hook context,
so the NO proves `systemMessage` stays out of it.
- [x] **Shown in the interactive UI:** `claude --plugin-dir <copy named
84b2bf30f3ee>` in a terminal showed, below the startup notices,
`SessionStart:startup says: Plugin mission desatualizado: instalado
84b2bf30f3ee, publicado e316a24e9826. Para atualizar, rode no shell
claude plugin update mission@brunoccalmeida-plugins e depois
/reload-plugins (ou abra uma sessão nova).` It shows a moment after the
banner, since interactive `SessionStart` hooks run in the background
([Hooks reference,
SessionStart](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md#sessionstart)).

